<title>INDIA: India raises rail freight rates for most items.</title>
<headline>India raises rail freight rates for most items.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Railways plans to raise freight rates for all commodities, barring essentials, by 12 percent for all distances, the Press Trust of India (PTI) quoted Railway Minister Ram Vilas Paswan as saying on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Presenting the railway budget for 1997/98 in parliament Paswan said a number of essential commodities including foodgrains and pulses, edible oils, kerosene, sugar, liquefied petroleum gas (LPG), fruits and jaggery have been exempted from the freight hike.</p>
<p>The increased rates would come into force from April 1, 1997, Paswan said.</p>
